From: Armada OS <armada@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wcd934x: clear the compander HALT bit on enable/disable

wcd934x_config_compander() sets WCD934X_COMP_HALT in the POST_PMD path
but nothing ever clears it: the PRE_PMU path only enables the clock and
toggles soft reset.  After the first power-down of an interpolator with
its compander enabled, every subsequent power-up runs the compander
clocked but halted (COMPANDERn_CTL0 reads 0x65) — it stops producing
gain data, so speakers behind a DRE-mode WSA881x play at the gain-word
floor and output is severely attenuated.

Any early PCM open/close cycle (PipeWire opening the card at boot before
UCM applies the routing) latches this state, making quiet speakers the
default on every boot.

Clear HALT after the soft-reset toggle on enable, and drop it again at
the end of the disable sequence to match the downstream (tavil) driver,
whose disable path ends by clearing HALT.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd934x.c
@@ -4228,6 +4228,9 @@
 		snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp, comp_ctl0_reg,
 					      WCD934X_COMP_SOFT_RST_MASK,
 					      WCD934X_COMP_SOFT_RST_DISABLE);
+		/* A previous disable leaves the compander halted */
+		snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp, comp_ctl0_reg,
+					      WCD934X_COMP_HALT_MASK, 0x0);
 		snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp, rx_path_cfg0_reg,
 					      WCD934X_HPH_CMP_EN_MASK,
 					      WCD934X_HPH_CMP_ENABLE);
@@ -4249,6 +4252,8 @@
 					      WCD934X_COMP_CLK_EN_MASK, 0x0);
 		snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp, comp_ctl0_reg,
 					      WCD934X_COMP_SOFT_RST_MASK, 0x0);
+		snd_soc_component_update_bits(comp, comp_ctl0_reg,
+					      WCD934X_COMP_HALT_MASK, 0x0);
 		break;
 	}
 
